+++ b/model/docs/paired-checkout.md
@@ -0,0 +1,81 @@
+# Paired CI checkout
+
+CI admission is pending. The renewed standalone source checkpoint is local commit
+`58a6989fe5ccd6a1ae734326d568f60dce2dab43`.
+It is not published or fetchable from `temporalio/umpire` and is not an admitted
+CI pin. The destination's read authorization remains unresolved (the recorded
+SSO 403 and CLI 401 do not establish access). No active workflow has been switched
+by this preparation.
+
+## Prepared setup interface
+
+[prepare-paired-checkout](../../.github/actions/prepare-paired-checkout/action.yml)
+accepts three explicit inputs: the accessible repository identity, one admitted full
+40-character commit SHA, and a credential authorized to read that repository. It
+has no default repository, revision or token. A repository-scoped `github.token`
+and existing GitHub App credentials must not be assumed to have cross-repository
+access. The credential source and fork-PR behavior need an owner-approved decision
+before activation; no secret name has been invented here.
+
+Run the action after the ordinary Temporal checkout and Go setup, before any root
+module download, package inspection, build or test. It temporarily checks out
+Umpire inside `github.workspace` to respect checkout's path constraint, then moves
+it beside the Temporal checkout. It leaves Temporal at `github.workspace`, so
+existing relative workflow paths, local actions, caches and artifact paths keep
+their meaning. The checkout does not persist its credential.
+
+The action requires unused sibling and parent workspace destinations. It refuses
+existing checkouts, `go.work` and `go.work.sum`, preserving their contents rather
+than modifying a shared runner workspace. It creates a parent `go.work` with these
+four modules and exports its absolute path through `GOWORK`:
+
+- the checked-out Temporal server root;
+- sibling `umpire/hosts/go`;
+- sibling `umpire/reference/kettle`;
+- Temporal's `model/temporal/hosts/go`.
+
+It reports both actual checked-out commit IDs and `go env GOWORK`. Go module
+resolution, Cargo metadata, native commands, generated protobuf freshness and
+current-pair guest evidence remain separate admission checks. Pinned tool setup
+still belongs to the invoking workflow; this action neither installs Rust/mise nor
+builds guests. See the sibling framework's `docs/consumer-interface.md` for the
+source seam.
+
+## Workflow activation map
+
+All root Go consumers need the sibling source even when a particular package does
+not import Umpire: module graph loading can encounter the root local replacement.
+The active checkout convention currently keeps Temporal at `github.workspace`.
+Apply the setup before the first dependency-consuming step in each relevant job:
+
+| Workflow or shared action | Affected entry points |
+| --- | --- |
+| `umpire.yml` | `framework`, `model`, `portability`, `canary`. Run the framework job's mise setup and gate from the sibling root. The paired Model job keeps `make model-check` in Temporal. Preserve the Go/live/canary checks. |
+| `run-tests.yml` | `pre-build`, `misc-checks`, `unit-test`, `leak-test`, `integration-test`, `functional-test`, `mixed-brain-test`; also notification jobs that execute root-module Go tools. Git/JQ-only setup and aggregate status jobs need no sibling source. |
+| `run-single-test.yml` | Unit and functional test jobs, before their module download/test commands. |
+| `linters.yml` | Go-backed tooling, protobuf tooling, workflowcheck, nilaway, format, parallelization and golangci jobs. Setup precedes module-consuming Make targets and tool installation where applicable. |
+| `govulncheck.yml`, `check-release-dependencies.yml`, `trigger-api-release.yml` | Vulnerability/module-graph checks and root-module dependency tools. Preserve existing public-action and release permissions. |
+| `flaky-tests-report.yml`, `ci-success-report.yml`, `optimize-test-sharding.yml` | Root-module Go reporting/sharding tools. Existing reporting credentials are not evidence of Umpire read access. |
+| `features-integration.yml`, `build-and-publish.yml`, `docker-build-manual.yml` | Jobs calling `build-binaries` or `build-docker-images`; account for helpers built from the root Go module. Preserve release and image publication behavior. |
+| `prepare-go/action.yml` | Setup must precede `go mod download`. Since this action also installs Go, separate its Go setup from module download or add paired setup between those steps when activating. |
+| `build-binaries/action.yml`, `build-docker-images/action.yml`, `post-test-reporting/action.yml` | Callers must retain the sibling checkout/workspace through binary, image-helper and post-test tool compilation. |
+
+When activating, use the same admitted standalone revision in every affected job
+and include both revisions and relevant lockfiles in cache provenance. Keep the
+independent standalone job independent of Temporal; paired jobs establish actual
+Temporal consumption. Existing root Go caches currently key only Temporal inputs
+and need review before reuse for the pair.
+
+## Remaining admission
+
+Supply a published exact standalone pin and demonstrate read access using the
+intended CI identity, including the supported pull-request contexts. Then wire the
+prepared action into affected jobs and review the resulting complete workflow
+source. A missing private-repository credential cannot be represented as a skipped
+successful gate or a fallback to retained in-tree framework source.
+
+Collect current paired checkout/module-resolution,
+required backend, protobuf-generation, guest-freshness and local-edit proofs from
+fn-258. The retired fn-257 evidence remains historical. This document and the
+unused composite action are source preparation only;
+no CI job or local gate was executed. Scala retirement remains separate fn-256 work.
